  "title": "Persian Constitutional Revolution",
  "summary": "In 1906 Mozafar o-Din Shah of Persia, forced by opposition to corruption and foreign manipulation, issued a decree for a constitution and an elected parliament, the Majlis; Belgium's constitution served as the model for the Fundamental Law. On 24 June 1908 the shah placed the Majlis under siege and bombarded it, and the struggle continued until the second Majlis ended in December 1911.",
